DESCRIPTION:National Coffee Day falls on September 29 in the United States\
 , and what it mostly consists of is free coffee: chains and roasters use t
 he date for giveaways and discounts. Nobody has documented who created it 
 or why the date is September 29. The adjacent International Coffee Day\, o
 n October 1\, does have a paper trail\, and the contrast between the two i
 s the most interesting thing about either.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/
 holiday/national-coffee-day/
